  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="12c1-ffce-0379-d334" name="Street Weapons" hidden="false">
      <description>Brutal gangs fight with fists and feet or easily concealed weapons. Clubs are short weapons (daggers, bludgeons, tyre irons; any long weapon counts as short). Spades are unarmed (fists, feet, brass knuckles, broken bottles); having little reach, unarmed attacks do not win drawn Exchanges against short weapons. Instead, when an unarmed attack triples the opponent's score it uses the Beat Down! rule rather than Overpower.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1b92-0311-0d49-7052" name="Beat Down!" hidden="false">
      <description>When an attacker uses a Beat Down instead of Overpower, no additional wounds are caused. Instead the winner of the Exchange immediately receives 1 Honour Point from the loser.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d3f4-7ebf-5e4a-2d70" name="No Missile Weapons" hidden="false">
      <description>Brutal warbands may not include units of Missile Troops. Units may still buy Throwing Weapons. (Not true of Wasteland Warriors.)</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="0bbf-1e39-adad-e5e4" name="Toughs" hidden="false">
      <description>Toughs are the TRIBAL Warriors under another name: they share all the usual rules, costs and Skills.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5578-a7ff-29c9-37de" name="Mighty Blow" hidden="false">
      <description>Characters only. When an unarmed Character triples the opponent's score, it makes a Mighty Blow instead of an Overpower: the wounds inflicted are doubled and the winner takes 1 Honour from the loser.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9d82-f268-7d2c-c80f" name="Firearms and Super Powers" hidden="false">
      <description>A firearm may be played as a stun weapon or as a super power. Skills such as Strong or Agile can represent low-level super abilities.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8ac3-e24b-6eeb-75cd" name="Villainous Chief" hidden="false">
      <description>Villainous Chiefs never fight without the protection of expendable Henchmen, so they cannot be fielded alone. Heroic warbands cannot include Toughs.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
